          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:bc3560fdf990a036af4a624d19a5658f87e2d9ec755a0306a76449761e343640:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://tests/test_checkpoints.py#L68-L77",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:fbb28fd09aa44539689811dd788c1c7cbae30708a6eefc182cb0fe24feff60e1:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_6a49831b0ce54223b8f5581993e42dd1",
      "statement": "Every /v1/audit/head, /v1/audit/log, /v1/audit/checkpoints, /v1/audit/verify and /v1/agents/{fp}/audit response is served through _send_signed with headers X-HAAP-Directory-Signature (b64 Ed25519 signature of the directory key over the canonical JSON of the exact body, via AuditService.sign_body) and X-HAAP-Directory-Fingerprint, so a consumer holding the directory public key can detect a rewrite of anything it already fetched; consumers SHOULD verify audit responses before trusting them.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/SPEC.md#L119-L119",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b514a23cb3ad9689b3ae3807ffc37da8a070837b791b23f3b98b22749c65039f:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/haap_directory/audit_service.py#L40-L42",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:41f1fe892aff6819e8e553353fa74a0f12ed89bc5dc746e83f1ba27a574d221c:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/haap_directory/http_api.py#L160-L166",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4dff09bfece92455275220b7621ff9dc43187428cff432fb84fca47c8936f57c:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_03309018d5674abcbdbcaaef739f4bc3",
      "statement": "The chain is tamper-evident, not tamper-proof: it detects a rewrite only for parties who fetched a signed checkpoint before the rewrite; it does not catch omission (checkpoints sign the chain, not the world); consumers who never fetch checkpoints get no protection at all; and the rewrite-detection window is bounded by the polling interval. The consumer duty is to poll /v1/audit/head at least as often as the checkpoint cadence and to escalate to a mirror.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/OPERATE.md#L80-L82",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:28104e9b7fac5eba6e5dca74a4ce082a21617c1a91c775ebe14a42dca9fafcc5:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/SPEC.md#L537-L544",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a2d5721730676a7cacbbc2192881a51536cf1ed3cbd245e920eec4330925ac53:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_4ba48bb8f6a34700a1341303e313c8c4",
      "statement": "The audit endpoints are the mirror ingest seam: mirror.ingest_chain pages /v1/audit/log until a short or empty batch, verifies the concatenated entries locally with audit.verify_chain, fetches /v1/audit/head and reports {seq, entry_hash, entries, verified, matches_served_head}; the helper never verifies the X-HAAP-Directory-Signature headers itself. Mirrors that agree on a head prove they saw the same ordered world.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/haap_directory/mirror.py#L25-L54",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:09afd30135c61acbb8f6357a9b933c5b0ae81f6e715c32a8cc42fe2078842945:"
        },
        {
